# Files that ship inside the APK byte-for-byte must not depend on the platform they
# were checked out on. Without this, a clone on Windows with core.autocrlf=true gets
# CRLF, the build packages CRLF, and the APK differs from one built on Linux — which
# was measured, not guessed: it accounted for every difference between two release
# builds except the .pyc headers. See docs/reproducible-builds.md.
#
# Deliberately narrow. Kotlin sources are compiled, and a release build from a CRLF
# checkout produced a byte-identical APK, so they are left alone.

# Chaquopy packages these verbatim into assets/chaquopy/app.imy
*.py text eol=lf

# Bundled as raw resources and read at runtime (license_mpl2.txt becomes res/S_.txt)
app/src/main/res/raw/** text eol=lf

# Run by CI and by the quality gates; CRLF breaks them on Linux
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Windows launcher already lives in the repository with CRLF and Windows needs it
# that way. Marked as untouched rather than as text-with-CRLF: declaring it text would
# renormalise the stored blob and rewrite all 93 lines for no behavioural change.
*.bat -text
